WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.769
 Well, gentlemen, it is
now down to the two of you

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.704
guys to battle it out for
the title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.438
champion.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.173
And so congratulations.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.075
In this final round, we're
going to be sending you guys

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.811
back home to build an
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:15.415
And that weapon is--

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.416
the Dahomey machete.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.353
MAN (VOICEOVER):
This lethal machete

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.122
was once wielded by the
legendary all-female army

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.793
in Western Africa known
as the Dahomey Amazons.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.029
The long, slightly curved
blade flared out to a wide tip,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.664
giving the female
warriors the ability

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:35.668
to deliver fatal blows that cut
cleanly through bone and flesh

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.136
in a single blow.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:40.106
These skilled women warriors
were an elite fighting force

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:43.108
and extremely intimidating,
often carrying trophies

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:44.778
of their fallen enemies.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.312
The machetes were
a powerful weapon

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:49.282
designed to cleave through
anything that got in their way.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:53.252
Today, the Dahomey machete can
be seen wielded in the 2020 HBO

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.121
series, "Lovecraft Country."

00:00:56.221 --> 00:00:57.457
GRADY POWELL: You guys
will have four days

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.791
to work on your
blades, because I

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:02.629
want you to both bring us back
a blade worth at least $10,000.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.829
We'll see you guys in four days.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:04.664
 All right.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.798 line:14%
 All right, good luck, man.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.032 line:14%
My name is Alex Morris.

00:01:07.132 --> 00:01:08.200 line:14%
I'm 48 years old.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.402
I'm from Warwick, Rhode Island.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.771
What I like most about
bladesmithing is it's

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.006 line:14%
challenging.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:16.142 line:8%
And I believe that if we
don't challenge ourselves,

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.409
we don't grow.

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:19.745
I'm super excited to
get after this thing.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.380
And in goes the steel.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.983
The biggest challenge
will be drawing

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.619
out the end of the blade.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.753
This is new for me.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.290
I'm-- probably going to take
me a while to figure out how

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.624
I'm going to move
this steel, to get

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.060
it to where I want it to go.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.195
Yeah, I'm liking it.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.162
It's getting there.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.530
I want to make
Damascus and build it

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:40.833
for the two disc-shaped
guards and hopefully

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.268
heat-treat my blade.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.770
Gonna stick some weld on there.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.372
And I'm going to get it in
the forge after I quench.

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:58.618
Yeah, yeah, it's looking good.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:01:59.552
Think we're good!

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.588
I think my blade is
coming out pretty well.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.156
Right now, I'm cleaning
up my Damascus.

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:06.059
If none of the knives
break out there,

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.194
they're going to start
looking at those things.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:13.966
The Damascus will help my
blade stand out against Adam's.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.602
Ah, it broke in half.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.306
The last forge weld I did last
night must not have taken.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:24.910
So I'm going to scrap it,
just use regular mono steel.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.845
Now I'm, like, starting
over completely

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.180
on my guards and pommel.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:31.050
So I wasted a lot of
time doing that Damascus,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.418
and it turned out for nothing.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:33.953
This is a hard challenge, man.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.387
This is taxing.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:36.222
Whew!

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.760 line:8%
ADAM: My name is Adam Coonradt,
and I'm a firefighter-paramedic

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.929 line:14%
in the city of Troy, New York.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.064
My wife and my kids
are very supportive,

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.399
and like that I do knifemaking.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.768
My two children, they're
both makers as well.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.404
And I couldn't be any
prouder of both of them.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.506
I have never made
anything this big before.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.341
If I win, I'm going
to Disneyland.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.043
I think right now,
my biggest obstacle

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.444
is the size of the piece.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.813
This piece of metal is
so thick and so large,

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:02.715
it's taking forever to heat up--

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.183
just not moving.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.818
I'm growing impatient.

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.086
I think there's
enough steel here,

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.721
I can actually cut off a piece.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.658
It's starting to move, but
very nervous about how thin

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.394
this blade actually
is starting to become.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.930
I don't want it to
break or shatter.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.270
I put some pressure on it
with the angle grinder.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.573
I ended up doing too much
pressure, and it broke.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.641
My heart sinks.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.476
Now, I have to restart.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:36.448
There's no way I can send
this in to be tested.

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:37.617
[sigh]

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.653
Day four-- final day,
make it or break it.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.188
So yesterday, I definitely
made a comeback.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:45.291
It's time to assemble.

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:47.393
Now, I started working on
my actual physical handle.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.028
I just don't want to
use a piece of wood.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.997
I want to dress it
up a little bit.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.466
So I twist three
different strands of wire,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.135
so it's going to have
an alternating pattern.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.870
The handle is looking great.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.639
It's better than I imagined.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.874
My kids came downstairs
to check on me.

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.175
 How's the machete
coming along?

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.177
 Aw, that's really cool.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.344
- You like that?
- Yeah.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.746
ADAM: Yeah, I can tell
they're proud of me,

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.749
sticking it through, and
being able to produce

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.816
a tangible item.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:11.918
It's a proud dad moment.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.152
 (DOUG MARCAIDA
VOICE) It will kill.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.421
 (DOUG MARCAIDA
VOICE) It will kill?

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.658
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.427
I will take your machete and
deliver some lethal blows

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.396
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.263
Alex, you're up first.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.030
You ready for this?

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:27.333
 Yes, sir.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.035
I'm most concerned about
everything with this test.

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.004
I'm not sure it's sharp enough.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:33.739
I'm not sure it's strong enough.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.775
I don't know what it's
going to do to my blade.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:36.676
I have no idea.

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:01.633
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Alex.

00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:04.137
The balance you have
in your blade is nice.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.305
For every cut, I can
really control and feel

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:07.807
like I'm chopping in there.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:09.508
The edge, no issues at all.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.177
It is still very sharp.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.111
More importantly,
sir, your machete--

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.713
it will kill.

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:15.647
 Thanks.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:16.816
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Adam, it's time

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:17.917
to have fun with your blade.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:18.684
Are you ready, sir?

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.220
 Yes, sir.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.755
I hope my blade doesn't break.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.557
I had a lot of setbacks
making this blade.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:25.791
You know, I had to start over.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:27.660
I hope it doesn't come back
to bite me in the butt.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.762
I'm saying a little
prayer-- please don't break,

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.731
please don't break,
please don't break.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:49.882
 (WHISPERING) Yes!

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.154
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Adam, let's talk

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.288
about your weapon here.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.658
This is a very
forward-heavy blade.

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:02.494
But that forward
weight really cuts deep

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:04.396
into this ballistics dummy.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:07.966
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:08.968
 That's worth it right there.

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:09.769
I can go home now.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.770
 [laughs]

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.974
 All right, gentlemen,
you know what time it is.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:18.978
It's time for the strength
test-- the shield chop.

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:21.113
What I want to see on top
of how durable your blades

00:06:21.179 --> 00:06:24.416
are-- is there effectiveness
against that shield, all right?

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:26.018
So Alex, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.786
 Yes, sir.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:48.874
 All right, so Alex, obviously,
there's a bit of an issue.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:52.145
What happened here is you--
you can see the grain size.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:55.581
It looks like 40
grit sandpaper, which

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:58.250
is really, really large grain.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:01.320
And then right here,
see that black?

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.922
 Yeah.
DAVID BAKER: That was a crack.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.056
 OK.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:05.958
 So that crack existed
probably during the heat treat.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:09.695
Once I hit just face onto the
shield, it just cut loose.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:17.303
GRADY POWELL: Alex,
we hate to see that.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:18.904
Your blade had a
catastrophic failure,

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.739
but you are not out
of the fight just yet.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.808
Your blade broke on
the fourth strike.

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:24.776
So that means, Adam, in order
to become "Forged in Fire"

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:28.247
champion, your Dahomey machete
must survive four strikes.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:28.981
Are you ready?

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.250
 Yes.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.485 line:8%
Everything is riding
on these four strikes.

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:35.821 line:8%
I need my machete
to hold together.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:37.289
I've got to make
it through this.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.124
Whew.

00:07:59.911 --> 00:08:01.813
GRADY POWELL: Well, Adam, you
survived your four strikes.

00:08:01.913 --> 00:08:03.649
So that means you are
the "Forged in Fire"

00:08:03.715 --> 00:08:05.751
champion, so congratulations.

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:08.787
Alex, unfortunately, you
didn't win this round.

00:08:08.887 --> 00:08:10.822
You crushed it in round
one and round two.

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:12.258
But your time in
the forge has ended.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.492
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:08:13.592 --> 00:08:16.295
step off the forge floor.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:17.530
 Thanks.

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.398
I'm a little disappointed,
but I'm definitely proud

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.100
of the machete that I made.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.435
Making something this big
was quite a challenge,

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:24.770
and it's a learning process.

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:27.473
So I'm definitely glad
I had this opportunity.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.307
I'm glad I got to know
all these other smiths.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:30.175
This was fun.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.043
It was a blast.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.248
 Well, Adam, your blade
survived the four strikes.

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:37.617
It's a beautiful beast.

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:40.786
And it just won you $10,000 and
the title of "Forged in Fire"

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:41.353
champion.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.222
Congratulations, man.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.357
Well done.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.025
Was it everything you
thought it would be?

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:47.059
ADAM: And more.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:47.960
It's been an honor.

00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:48.994
It's been a pleasure.

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:51.263
Wow, what an experience.

00:08:51.363 --> 00:08:52.297
It's kind of surreal.

00:08:52.364 --> 00:08:53.432
But it's a great feeling.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.700
It's awesome.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:57.937
My family supported me, so
kids, we're going to Disney.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:09:01.541
[music playing]

